      "side": 1,
      "message": "The call-stack you shared relies on ACPI parsing  (`early_acpi_boot_init()` -\u003e `default_acpi_madt_oem_check()`), which is active in the primary Microdroid kernel (which has `CONFIG_ACPI\u003dy`). However, the secondary crashdump kernel is built with CONFIG_ACPI deliberately disabled. So `early_acpi_boot_init()` and `acpi_boot_init()` are empty stubs and `x2apic_acpi_madt_oem_check` will not be called.\n\nNevertheless, setting `x2apic_phys` would actually work since `x86_64_probe_apic` called during late probe in `time_init` will use it and this happens indeed before the interrupts are enabled.\n\nI will drop this patch and instead prepare one setting x2apic_phys via commandline",
