      "writtenOn": "2026-09-07T11:29:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My bad: aosp/4248642 doesn\u0027t really fix the issue (I thought it did because a few test iterations passed (I was \"lucky\" that during those tests timer irq didn\u0027t hit in vulnerable window between irq enabled and switch to x2apic phys) but when repeated many times I hit the issue again).\n\nSo this patch is still needed.\n\nAbove I wrote:\n\n\u003e Nevertheless, setting x2apic_phys would actually work since x86_64_probe_apic called during late probe in time_init will use it and this happens indeed before the interrupts are enabled.\n\nand this was my mistake: `time_init`, only assigns `x86_late_time_init` (which finally calls `x86_64_probe_apic`) as   `late_time_init`. But `late_time_init` is actually called after `local_irq_enable` (see: `start_kernel`).\n\nI\u0027ve updated the commit log a bit and rebased. I think we indeed should try to upstream it (after removing ANDROID specific commit log details).",
