      "writtenOn": "2026-08-21T13:18:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is actually related to kind of exotic pKVM setup. This issue was found because:  `com.android.microdroid.test.MicrodroidHostTests#testTombstonesAreGeneratedUponKernelCrash_protectedVm_true_os_microdroid` is failing. The same test for `protectedVm_false` is passing even without this patch.\n\nIt is because pKVM for pVMs enforces using x2apic mode (aosp/3982019) and explicitly forbids transitioning a pVM out of x2APIC mode: https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/3982019/7/arch/x86/kvm/lapic.c. This causes the guest kernel to skip mapping the APIC MMIO fixmap page.\n\nAlso, as you know, even if APIC MMIO will be mapped and not skipped, we could not use MMIO-based APIC as we do not have (and rather do not want to have) instruction decoding support in pKVM. And because the crashdump kernel doesn\u0027t enable CONFIG_ACPI, the default APIC is MMIO based, which can\u0027t work under pKVM.\n\nAnyway, I think that what Chuanxiao suggested (setting x2apic_phys via commandline), is simpler and works as well. So I will probably drop this patch and go with such direction.",
      "parentUuid": "7f9e8ab0_33491010",
      "revId": "e5ed6ab8e9191b78d2c4cafca005e7c12ee244d4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
